Problem with: kernel 2.6.4 (also 2.6.3) module: 8250_pnp (and all 8250_*)
When I load or compile into kernel this module (or any of 8250_*) it cannot 
discover my RS-232 port, which is on my internal isa pnp modem card. The 
serial port is normal UART16550A on 0x02f8-th port and 3-rd irq.

I have isa pnp modem card: 'Texas Instruments V.34+ FAX Internal' with pnp 
signature: 'TEX0011' and sub signature: 'TEX0000'. This modem signature 
(TEX0011) is supported by '8250_pnp', I found it into file:  
'linux-2.6.4/drivers/serial/8250_pnp.c'.

Also I saw no file '/proc/bus/isapnp/devices', I don't know, if it is a 
problem.

In the attachment I send you some files: from my '/proc' directory, and also 
from '/proc' form kernel 2.4.25 in which it working without any 
problems(module serial). There are also configs  files and dmesgs outputs. I 
haven't patched any kernels. 



